  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe `<fieldset>` element is specified to generate an [anonymous fieldset content box](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#anonymous-fieldset-content-box) which inherits a set of properties from the `<fieldset>` element. Among that list of properties is `column-rule` which will then apply if the content box is a grid, flexbox, or multicol container.\n\n[CSS Gap Decorations](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-gaps-1/) introduces `row-rule` and subproperties `row-rule-width`, `row-rule-style`, and `row-rule-color` which function exactly the same as the corresponding `column-rule-*` properties, but in the row direction. As such, I suggest adding `row-rule` to the list of properties that inherit from a `<fieldset>` to its anonymous fieldset content box.",
